# attention_top formal: BMC over the module's own `ifdef FORMAL block
# (rtl/attention_top.sv, docs/uarch.md 8.3 "FORMAL block" paragraph).
# Scope is deliberately control-only per CLAUDE.md ("formal is a subset /
# do not fight the tool") and per uarch.md 8.3's own statement of the
# property list: reset state (S_IDLE, busy=0, done=0, cycle_count=0),
# busy/done mutual exclusion, done implies idle, cycle_count monotone
# non-decreasing while busy, and (2026-09-18) lane_out_valid one-hot-or-zero
# (the invariant the shared PV datapath relies on). None of these reference
# q_mem/k_mem/v_mem/out_mem, the NUM accumulators, the score/rescale
# arithmetic, or the divider bank; the control FSM's transition conditions
# depend only on counters (t, kb, rg, row, div_cnt) and start, never on
# datapath values.
#
# DEPTH (2026-09-18, review finding F013): the previous single task ran at
# depth 10 from `initial assume (rst)`. The shortest legal run (n_len = 4)
# is 173 cycles, so `done` could never be 1 inside any depth-10 trace: the
# "done implies idle" property and the done half of busy/done exclusion were
# VACUOUS, and EVIDENCE audit-attention_top-formal-coverage's "non-vacuous"
# wording was wrong for them (see EVIDENCE.md errata). Two tasks now:
#   prove : mode bmc, depth 180, with the RTL FORMAL block assuming n_len = 4
#           on the accepted start so completion is reachable inside the bound.
#   cover : mode cover, depth 180, `cover (done)` in the RTL: sby must reach
#           done or the task fails, which is the machine check that `prove`
#           exercises the completion properties. Both tasks are required.
# Runtime at depth 180 has NOT been measured (no toolchain on the machine
# that made this change); yices completed depth 10 in 2.8 s after the BRAM
# conversion. If depth 180 is intractable, keep this file's tasks and record
# the achieved depth honestly rather than silently lowering it.
#
# Inner-module assertions are stripped below (chformal -assert -remove on
# mac_unit, matmul_tile, online_softmax) because each of those contracts is
# already proven standalone and auditor-countersigned (formal/mac_unit.sby,
# formal/matmul_tile.sby, formal/online_softmax.sby, all PASS, EVIDENCE.md
# rows). Re-proving them again inside this integration-level BMC would be
# redundant solver load for zero additional coverage: the three submodules
# are instantiated here UNMODIFIED (uarch.md 8.3's own words).
#
# What is NOT proven here, and why that is fine: the running-max-monotonic
# and DEN-no-overflow invariants for the (m, l) recurrence are proven
# standalone in formal/online_softmax.sby; the NUM accumulator's own
# no-overflow bound (uarch.md 3.7) and the divider bank's arithmetic
# (uarch.md 3.8) are exercised end-to-end, bit-exactly, by cocotb
# (tb/attention_top/test_attention_top.py) against model/attn.py
# attn_fixed, not re-attempted in formal.
#
# Solver: z3 hangs >10 min on this memory-heavy model (3 RAMs + ROM +
# 16-wide divider bank still in the transition relation), independent of
# the BMC depth target; yices completes (trials 2026-07-16).
[tasks]
prove
cover

[options]
prove: mode bmc
prove: depth 180
cover: mode cover
cover: depth 180

[engines]
smtbmc yices

[script]
read_verilog -sv -formal -DFORMAL mac_unit.sv matmul_tile.sv online_softmax.sv attention_top.sv
prep -top attention_top
chformal -assert -remove mac_unit
chformal -assert -remove matmul_tile
chformal -assert -remove online_softmax

[files]
rtl/mac_unit.sv
rtl/matmul_tile.sv
rtl/online_softmax.sv
rtl/attention_top.sv
rtl/exp_lut.svh rtl/exp_lut.svh
